        "heading": "Conditions and Treatment Options",
        "body": "Elbow pain can originate from a variety of tissues in the body — muscle bellies, tendons, bursae, ligaments, bones, cartilage and nerves. It may also stem from more than one cause, meaning a patient can have several coexisting conditions at once. Physiotherapist Konstantinos Danalis assesses each patient in line with international clinical guidelines and identifies the tissues likely to be responsible for the pain, so that treatment can be precisely targeted."
