        "heading": "What Is a Tendon?",
        "body": "A muscle is made up of a central part — the muscle belly — which contracts and produces movement at a joint, and its peripheral parts, which act like ropes and attach to a bone: these are the tendons. A tendon works both like a rope and like a stiff spring; it has a small amount of give in its length and can store energy. The tendon is composed of long collagen fibres wrapped in connective tissue — like small ropes — and together they form the larger structure, the tendon."
